-- ============================================================
-- V139: Pre-production seed data baseline (skillars-deferred-112)
--
-- Companion to V138 (which is pure DDL, zero DML). Reproduces the FINAL
-- state of every table any pre-squash migration seeded, generated with
-- `pg_dump --data-only --no-owner --column-inserts --on-conflict-do-nothing`
-- against the same reference database as V138 (V02..V137, pre-squash commit
-- 4a3f218dabd04e0c8419282e922f60de5f93934d) -- not by concatenating the
-- historical INSERT statements. See docs/deployment/migration-rebaseline.md
-- for the full per-table rationale; summary:
--
--   main.authority          5 rows  -- ROLE_COACH/PARENT/PLAYER/ADMIN/LTD_ADMIN.
--                                      ids 100-104 preserved verbatim: they are
--                                      FK targets of user_authority.authority_id.
--   main.platform_config  120 rows  -- id column dropped (V128 made it an
--                                      identity column; MigrationLint's
--                                      PLATFORM_CONFIG_EXPLICIT_ID rule exists
--                                      for exactly this reason, and it's correct
--                                      on the merits even though V139 itself
--                                      sits at the grandfather baseline and
--                                      isn't linted). updated_at column dropped
--                                      (defaults to now()); a literal dump-time
--                                      timestamp has no business meaning here.
--   session.drills          20 rows -- ids preserved verbatim: V39 originally
--                                      seeded these with gen_random_uuid(), and
--                                      V111 exists solely to replace those
--                                      random ids with the deterministic ones
--                                      below (matched by trans_key). Copying
--                                      V39's inserts instead would silently
--                                      reintroduce the exact bug V111 fixed.
--                                      created_at/updated_at columns dropped
--                                      (both default to now()) for the same
--                                      reason as platform_config.updated_at.
--   development.skill_definitions
--                          15 rows  -- the radar skill catalog (PAC/SHO/PAS/...).
--
-- Every statement is `ON CONFLICT (<natural key>) DO NOTHING`, so re-running
-- this file against an already-seeded database inserts zero rows and raises
-- no error. The platform_config identity sequence is bumped past every id
-- that any pre-squash migration ever issued (606, not 121) so a freshly
-- application-generated config row can never collide with a historical id
-- that some external reference might still assume -- defensive, since none
-- is known to exist, but cheap.
--
-- main.authority.created_date uses NOW() rather than the literal dump-time
-- timestamp pg_dump captured, for the same reason updated_at/created_at are
-- dropped elsewhere: a frozen historical instant has no business meaning in
-- a baseline meant to be re-run fresh at any future date.
-- ============================================================





SELECT pg_catalog.setval('main.platform_config_id_seq', 606, true);
